{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `Y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: rewrote the repeated likelihood from a loop with indexed left-hand side `Y[n] ~ multi_normal(mu, Sigma)` to the equivalent vectorized statement `Y ~ multi_normal(mu, Sigma)`. This preserves the same summed multivariate-normal likelihood while making the protected observation a top-level plain identifier observed exactly once and outside control flow. No data changes were required.
","model_safe_stan":"// Jaws: repeated measures analysis of variance
//  http://www.openbugs.net/Examples/Jaws.html

data {
  int<lower=0> N;
  int<lower=0> M;
  array[N] vector[M] Y;
  array[M] real age;
  cov_matrix[M] S;
}
transformed data {
  real mean_age;
  mean_age = mean(age);
}
parameters {
  real beta0;
  real beta1;
  cov_matrix[M] Sigma;
}
transformed parameters {
  vector[M] mu;
  // for (m in 1:M) mu[m] <- beta0 + beta1 * (age[m] - mean_age); 

  for (m in 1 : M) {
    mu[m] = beta0 + beta1 * age[m];
  }
}
model {
  beta0 ~ normal(0, 32);
  beta1 ~ normal(0, 32);
  Sigma ~ inv_wishart(4, S);
  Y ~ multi_normal(mu, Sigma);
}
